          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "SP 91 NW                 PITSTONE 4/137                                        The Windmill (formerly listed                                              under Ivinghoe parish) 26.9.51 -                                            II* Windmill.  Dated 1627 and 1749, altered and much restored 1963.  Post-mill on circular base of C19 whitewashed brick with shallow conical roof of metal sheets.  2 doors.  Timber framed and weatherboarded chamber above has curved roof, double board doors with board hood on shaped brackets, and small board door to loft.  Sail side of chamber has central post with moulded wooden bracket.  4 sails.  Tail pole with wooden wheel, wide wooden step ladder.  Internal machinery is intact but probably C19, restored. (David Wray, Pitstone Windmill) Listing NGR: SP9451015677"
    }
